  b. Mark modified versions. A modified version must say clearly that it is
     modified and unofficial, and must use a name other than "Asphyxia-UI" on
     its own (for example "MyPack, based on Asphyxia-UI"). It must not suggest
     it is endorsed by, or comes from, the copyright holder.
  c. No money. No one may make money from Asphyxia-UI material or any work
     based on it without prior written permission from the copyright holder.
     This includes, among other things: selling it; charging for downloads,
     access, early access, support or installation; paywalls, subscriptions
     or membership-only content (such as Patreon tiers); donations, tips or
     sponsorships connected to it; advertising-supported or link-shortener
     download pages; and bundling it in a paid product or service.
  d. Same terms. Anything you share that contains Asphyxia-UI material must be
     shared under this same license, free of charge.

Written permission for commercial use may be requested from the copyright
holder and is granted only case by case. Permission given to one person does
not extend to anyone else.

If any condition is broken, the permissions in this license end for that
